{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix + AFTER measurements.\n\nBoth import-bound defaults are replaced with a NAMED indirection that resolves `time.sleep` at call time — `access_check._retry_sleep` and `dependency_audit._retry_sleep` — mirroring `acli_subprocess._backoff_sleep`, which the tree already carries for exactly this reason.\n\nNote on approach: the reviewed plan said `sleep_fn=None` plus an in-body `if sleep_fn is None`. That was implemented, and it FAILED the shrink-only complexity ratchet — the extra branch pushed `run_access_check` from 15 to 16 (`check_complexity_baseline --check`: `active=59 new=1`, exit 1), and that gate needs an administrator override to accept a new entry. The named indirection achieves the same late binding with no added branch; the gate is back to `active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`. Description not changed for this, since it is the same seam by a cheaper construction.\n\n| test | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_probe_retries_jql_search_three_times` (in module) | 25.01s | ~0s |\n| `test_gate_reports_db_unreachable_as_infrastructure` | 15.00s | ~0s |\n| `test_non_404_http_error_still_propagates` | 16.18s | 0.04s |\n\nAll three enclosing modules together: **68 passed in 2.08s** (1.03s user + 0.95s system). Aggregate saving **~56s of wall clock per suite run**, and it is wall clock that was previously pure idle — the CPU was doing nothing.\n\nEach test now RECORDS the backoff and asserts the logical schedule: `[5, 5, 5, 5, 5]`, `[5, 10]`, and for the jittered ADR-0036 path three delays each within `[2**(attempt+1), 2**(attempt+1)+1)`. Bounds rather than equalities there because the jitter is `random.random()`. No timing-budget assertion was added anywhere — `check_wall_clock_asserts` passes."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786604660855640001,"uuid":"979c3954-7a5c-45db-86c8-0276a5c98054"}